{
    "background_story": "Danna was a brilliant and eccentric oceanographer who spent her life studying the mysteries of the deep. Growing up near the coast, she was fascinated by the sea and its secrets. As she delved deeper into her research, Danna became particularly captivated by the planet Neptune, named after the Roman god of the sea. She saw parallels between the icy giant's turbulent storms and the ocean's own unpredictable nature. Danna's groundbreaking research on ocean currents and marine life earned her international recognition. She went on to lead several expeditions to explore the ocean's unknown regions, always keeping Neptune as her celestial inspiration. Her work helped raise awareness about the importance of marine conservation, and she became known as the 'Neptune's Daughter' among her peers.",
